    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d120">

                <pb facs="0235" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/425</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-19T14:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 19, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 23, 2.50 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1531. Quiet prevailed throughout yesterday and last night. Loyal troops arrived
                    from front, number unknown. Are now surrounding palace on other side Neva which
                    been headquarters Bolsheviks and which near Peter Paul
                    prison where Sturmer, Protopopov and others confined.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d120-f1"/> Reported that prison garrison will aid Bolsheviks if
                    resistance offered but uncertain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
